      "subject": "fix(org-tools): parse Brave news search results from the correct path",
      "body": "The server-side trusted-integration executor (the live path for workspace\nBrave search) shaped news results with `/{vertical}/results`, but Brave's\nNews API returns results at the top-level `results` array (envelope type\n\"news\", no `news` wrapper) — so news searches found nothing and silently\nreturned empty. Web search nests under `web.results` and was correct.\n\nUse a vertical-aware pointer: `/results` for news, `/{vertical}/results`\notherwise (web unchanged). Adds tests for both verticals (news had none).\n\nCompanion to the same fix in the secondary in-harness execution path.",
      "parents": [
